posterior mean is E(exp(XB)).  The former can also be approximated by
the posterior median.  If you report the MLE, you need to use the delta
method to give confidence intervals, etc. which may not be fun. 
Alternatively, you can report Bayesian confidence intervals by just
taking the 2.5th and 97.5th percentile of your simulation draws.  You
can also report either the posterior mean or posterior median.
  

  

Kosuke

